abstract: >-
  BoltZ-Kernel is a diagnostic solver for open quantum systems beyond the
  Lindblad (Markovian) approximation. It computes Boltzmann memory kernels
  K*(t, s) from an arbitrary spectral density J(ω) via the Jaynes
  Maximum-Entropy principle, solves the generalised integro-differential
  master equation, and quantifies the deviation from the standard Lindblad
  prediction. Covers Ohmic, super-Ohmic, Lorentzian (cavity QED),
  band-edge (photonic crystal), photonic-crystal-with-gap, and
  waveguide-QED environments; supports arbitrary J(ω) via CSV import,
  Python formula, or stdin. Exposes a PyQt6 GUI, a Unix-style CLI, and
  a YAML-driven batch pipeline sharing the same core engine. Dual-licensed
  (Apache-2.0 for academic / non-commercial use; proprietary for commercial).
